# Gone Fishing exiles its two targets together and returns them together (CR 608.2c, 101.4, 614.12): Blooming Marsh and Seachrome
# Coast ("enters tapped unless you control two or fewer other lands") each see only Forest and Island, so both come back untapped.
# Returned one after the other the second would see three other lands and enter tapped. Seachrome Coast came in tapped (a fourth
# land), so it was tapped when exiled; the new object is untapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Blooming Marsh
Seachrome Coast
Forest
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Lake-town Mariners
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Blooming Marsh.Play
? Bot1.Battlefield.Blooming Marsh.Tapped = false
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Seachrome Coast.Play
? Bot1.Battlefield.Seachrome Coast.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lake-town Mariners.Cast(Ability: Adventure)
Bot1.Target(Blooming Marsh; Seachrome Coast)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 7
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Blooming Marsh.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Seachrome Coast.Tapped = false
Exile = Lake-town Mariners
